            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Portuguese for the voluntary work, then the Portuguese for the charity."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: supor",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "supor — \"to suppose\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Suponho que ele já saiu de casa. I suppose he has already left home."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Conjugated like pôr: suponho, supões, supõe. Suponhamos que… — let us suppose that…"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "supor is inherited from Latin suppōnere \"to put or set under, to substitute\" (EtymDB, Lewis & Short), built from sub and pōnere \"to put\", and reshaped on pôr."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
